  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the dataset suggests that Eprosartan may be associated with Hypertensive Disorder through off-label use in the context of Diabetic Nephropathy. This association is supported by multiple pathways where Eprosartan is linked to Diabetic Nephropathy, which in turn is indicated for Hypertensive Disorder via different medications (Captopril, Losartan, and Irbesartan). The high scores across all three paths (final_score=0.6519) indicate a consistent and significant relationship, likely due to the shared clinical context of diabetic complications and their management with angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors or angiotensin II receptor blockers (ARBs). The recurring mechanism involves the use of off-label medications for managing diabetic nephropathy, which is a known risk factor for hypertension. While the evidence is strong, it is important to note that off-label use is not always approved or standardized, and the clinical relevance of these associations requires further validation through rigorous studies.",
